# Shell scripts must be LF in the blob AND in the working tree.
#
# Blob: scripts/update_fixs.sh is downloaded from raw.githubusercontent and run
# directly by a consuming app's bootstrap, so a CR in the shebang breaks it
# outright - the kernel reports "bash\r: no such file or directory".
#
# Working tree: the release zip is packed on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites *.sh to CRLF on checkout, so the bundle shipped CRLF scripts with no
# exec bit even though every blob was already LF. eol=lf overrides autocrlf for
# these files, which is what lets the installer's unpack-time CRLF normalization
# be retired once a release ships built from a checkout with this in place.
*.sh text eol=lf
